{
  "id": "0af209d3-d726-4efc-8e9a-093a95b41906",
  "sourceUrl": "https://docs.spring.io/spring-boot/3.5/reference/",
  "title": "Auto-configuration",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "auto-configuration-0",
      "type": "header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Auto-configuration"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "auto-configuration-0-point-0",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Auto-configuration is Boot\u2019s built-in configuration code for setting up framework objects your application needs."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "auto-configuration-0-point-1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "For example, Boot can create the objects that start Tomcat and connect incoming requests to Spring MVC."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "auto-configuration-0-point-2",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Your application does not need to declare each of those framework objects with its own "
        ],
        [
          "@Bean",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " method."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "auto-configuration-0-point-3",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "@SpringBootApplication",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " enables this mechanism through its included "
        ],
        [
          "@EnableAutoConfiguration",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " annotation."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "auto-configuration-0-point-4",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Boot applies this configuration during startup. It does not generate Java files in your project."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "auto-configuration-web-case",
      "type": "header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Spring Web case"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "auto-configuration-web-case-point-0",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "spring-boot-starter-web",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " brings in Spring MVC and embedded Tomcat libraries in this Boot version."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "auto-configuration-web-case-point-1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "The dependency makes those libraries available. Auto-configuration decides how to register and configure their framework objects."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "auto-configuration-web-case-point-2",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "A "
        ],
        [
          "ServletWebServerFactory",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " is a bean that creates the embedded servlet server. Boot supplies a Tomcat implementation for this project."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "auto-configuration-web-case-point-3",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "DispatcherServlet",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " is Spring MVC\u2019s central request dispatcher. It sends requests to the matching MVC handlers."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "auto-configuration-web-case-point-4",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Boot registers that dispatcher and the supporting MVC configuration."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "auto-configuration-web-case-point-5",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Boot does not write application controllers or business methods. A running server can therefore have no application endpoint."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "auto-configuration-conditions",
      "type": "header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Conditions"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "auto-configuration-conditions-point-0",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "An auto-configuration has checks called conditions. It applies only when its required checks pass."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "auto-configuration-conditions-point-1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "A class condition checks whether a required library class is available."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "auto-configuration-conditions-point-2",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "A bean condition checks whether the application has already supplied a particular kind of bean."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "auto-configuration-conditions-point-3",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "A property condition checks an application setting."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "auto-configuration-conditions-point-4",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "A web-application condition checks whether the application uses the required web environment."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "auto-configuration-conditions-point-5",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "For the Tomcat case, the relevant server libraries must be available and the application must be a servlet web application."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "auto-configuration-conditions-point-6",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "The default server-factory configuration also requires that the application has not already provided a "
        ],
        [
          "ServletWebServerFactory",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " bean."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "auto-configuration-condition-annotations",
      "type": "header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Condition annotations"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "auto-configuration-condition-annotations-point-0",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Boot expresses many checks with annotations on its configuration classes or bean methods."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "auto-configuration-condition-annotations-point-1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "@ConditionalOnClass",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " requires the specified classes to be available."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "auto-configuration-condition-annotations-point-2",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "@ConditionalOnMissingBean",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " requires the specified bean to be absent before the default is registered."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "auto-configuration-condition-annotations-point-3",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "@ConditionalOnProperty",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " checks a named property against the condition\u2019s declared rule."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "auto-configuration-condition-annotations-point-4",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "These annotations describe how Boot\u2019s defaults are selected. Ordinary application classes do not need them to receive auto-configuration."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "auto-configuration-lesson-1",
      "type": "header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Application overrides"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "auto-configuration-lesson-1-point-0",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Where Boot checks for a missing bean, declaring your own matching bean makes Boot skip that particular default."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "auto-configuration-lesson-1-point-1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "For example, a "
        ],
        [
          "@Bean",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " method returning a "
        ],
        [
          "ServletWebServerFactory",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " supplies the server factory explicitly."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "auto-configuration-lesson-1-point-2",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Boot\u2019s missing-bean check then prevents its default factory from being registered."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "auto-configuration-lesson-1-point-3",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "This selects the application\u2019s factory instead of creating two factories and choosing one with "
        ],
        [
          "@Primary",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          "."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "auto-configuration-lesson-1-point-4",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Other auto-configuration can still apply. Replacing one default does not disable the entire feature."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "auto-configuration-lesson-1-point-5",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "The replacement must satisfy that feature\u2019s requirements. An unrelated bean does not replace it."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "auto-configuration-source-comparison",
      "type": "header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Starters, scanning, and auto-configuration"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "auto-configuration-source-table",
      "type": "table",
      "columnOrder": [
        "0",
        "1"
      ],
      "hasColumnHeader": true,
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "auto-configuration-source-row-0",
          "type": "table_row",
          "cells": {
            "0": [
              [
                "Mechanism"
              ]
            ],
            "1": [
              [
                "Concrete role"
              ]
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "auto-configuration-source-row-1",
          "type": "table_row",
          "cells": {
            "0": [
              [
                "Starter"
              ]
            ],
            "1": [
              [
                "Adds libraries to the build."
              ]
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "auto-configuration-source-row-2",
          "type": "table_row",
          "cells": {
            "0": [
              [
                "Component scanning"
              ]
            ],
            "1": [
              [
                "Finds application components such as an annotated service."
              ]
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "auto-configuration-source-row-3",
          "type": "table_row",
          "cells": {
            "0": [
              [
                "Auto-configuration"
              ]
            ],
            "1": [
              [
                "Registers framework defaults when their conditions match."
              ]
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "auto-configuration-lesson-2",
      "type": "header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Condition report"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "auto-configuration-lesson-2-point-0",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "--debug",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " adds the condition evaluation report to the startup log."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "auto-configuration-lesson-2-point-1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Positive matches list configurations whose conditions passed."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "auto-configuration-lesson-2-point-2",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Negative matches identify configurations or bean methods that did not meet their conditions."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "auto-configuration-lesson-2-point-3",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "A negative match is often normal. For example, the application may not include the library for that feature."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "auto-configuration-lesson-2-point-4",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "The report gives the reason for each recorded decision. It is more specific than assuming every starter always enables every related feature."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "auto-configuration-lesson-2-example-0",
      "type": "example",
      "example": {
        "title": "Inspect the framework beans Boot supplies",
        "language": "text",
        "description": [
          "The two tabs contain the complete Maven build and application source.",
          "Java 17 or later and Maven must be installed.",
          "The command runs from the directory containing `pom.xml`.",
          "Port `8080` must be available.",
          "The application declares no server factory, dispatcher, or controller bean of its own."
        ],
        "code": "",
        "explanation": [
          "`pom.xml` supplies the Spring Web starter, which provides the MVC and Tomcat libraries.",
          "`SpringApplication.run` creates the application context and applies matching auto-configuration.",
          "`getBeansOfType` returns the managed beans implementing the requested type. The example prints their counts.",
          "The displayed lines are the expected counts for this application. Boot also writes startup logs and the condition report.",
          "The server-factory and dispatcher beans come from framework configuration, not from application `@Bean` methods.",
          "In the report, `ServletWebServerFactoryAutoConfiguration` relates to embedded-server setup.",
          "`WebMvcAutoConfiguration` relates to the MVC defaults.",
          "Each report entry explains the conditions that matched or prevented a particular configuration.",
          "The counts demonstrate registered framework objects. They do not demonstrate a working business endpoint.",
          "If the web starter is removed, the application no longer has the MVC types imported by this example and does not compile unchanged."
        ],
        "commands": "mvn spring-boot:run -Dspring-boot.run.arguments=--debug",
        "files": [
          {
            "name": "pom.xml",
            "language": "text",
            "code": "<project xmlns=\"http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0\" xmlns:xsi=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\"\n         xsi:schemaLocation=\"http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 https://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd\">\n    <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>\n    <parent>\n        <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>\n        <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-parent</artifactId>\n        <version>3.5.16</version>\n        <relativePath/>\n    </parent>\n    <groupId>com.example</groupId>\n    <artifactId>demo</artifactId>\n    <version>1.0.0</version>\n    <properties><java.version>17</java.version></properties>\n    <dependencies>\n        <dependency>\n            <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>\n            <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-web</artifactId>\n        </dependency>\n    </dependencies>\n    <build>\n        <finalName>demo</finalName>\n        <plugins>\n            <plugin>\n                <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>\n                <artifactId>spring-boot-maven-plugin</artifactId>\n            </plugin>\n        </plugins>\n    </build>\n\n</project>\n"
          },
          {
            "name": "src/main/java/com/example/demo/DemoApplication.java",
            "language": "java",
            "code": "package com.example.demo;\n\nimport org.springframework.boot.SpringApplication;\nimport org.springframework.boot.autoconfigure.SpringBootApplication;\nimport org.springframework.boot.web.servlet.server.ServletWebServerFactory;\nimport org.springframework.web.servlet.DispatcherServlet;\n\n@SpringBootApplication\npublic class DemoApplication {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        var context = SpringApplication.run(DemoApplication.class, args);\n\n        System.out.println(\"Server factory beans: \"\n                + context.getBeansOfType(ServletWebServerFactory.class).size());\n        System.out.println(\"MVC dispatcher beans: \"\n                + context.getBeansOfType(DispatcherServlet.class).size());\n    }\n}\n"
          }
        ],
        "result": "Server factory beans: 1\nMVC dispatcher beans: 1",
        "possibleOutput": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "auto-configuration-exclusions",
      "type": "header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Exclusions"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "auto-configuration-exclusions-point-0",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "An exclusion tells Boot not to apply a particular auto-configuration class."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "auto-configuration-exclusions-point-1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "The "
        ],
        [
          "exclude",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " attribute on "
        ],
        [
          "@SpringBootApplication",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " accepts auto-configuration class names as class literals."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "auto-configuration-exclusions-point-2",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "spring.autoconfigure.exclude",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " is the configuration-property alternative."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "auto-configuration-exclusions-point-3",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "An exclusion disables that configuration, not the library dependency."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "auto-configuration-exclusions-point-4",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Excluding configuration needed by the application can prevent startup or remove feature support."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "auto-configuration-exclusions-point-5",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "The condition report identifies the applicable configuration before an exclusion is considered."
        ]
      ]
    }
  ],
